From: RK3308BS M1SOC build <build@localhost>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: panel-simple: guard optional regulator in resume/suspend

Patch 0007 changed the panel "power" supply acquisition to
devm_regulator_get_optional() and maps the absent-supply case (-ENODEV)
to p->supply = NULL. Our RK3308 panel node has no power-supply, so
p->supply is NULL.

Stock panel_simple_resume()/panel_simple_suspend() call
regulator_enable(p->supply) / regulator_disable(p->supply)
unconditionally. That was safe with the original devm_regulator_get()
(non-NULL dummy regulator), but with the optional supply now NULL it
dereferences NULL -- regulator_enable() reads regulator->rdev on its
first line.

This is the exact crash seen at the first fbdev modeset commit (kernel
Oops 0000000096000004 in regulator_enable+0x38, called from
panel_simple_resume -> panel_simple_prepare ->
panel_bridge_atomic_pre_enable during drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail),
which hard-faulted display bring-up and froze the board on boot. The
probe-time regulator_enable() (patch 0009) was already guarded with
"if (panel->supply)"; this does the same for resume/suspend.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
@@ -308,7 +308,8 @@
 	struct panel_simple *p = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(p->enable_gpio, 0);
-	regulator_disable(p->supply);
+	if (p->supply)
+		regulator_disable(p->supply);
 	p->unprepared_time = ktime_get_boottime();
 
 	drm_edid_free(p->drm_edid);
@@ -342,10 +343,12 @@
 
 	panel_simple_wait(p->unprepared_time, p->desc->delay.unprepare);
 
-	err = regulator_enable(p->supply);
-	if (err < 0) {
-		dev_err(dev, "failed to enable supply: %d\n", err);
-		return err;
+	if (p->supply) {
+		err = regulator_enable(p->supply);
+		if (err < 0) {
+			dev_err(dev, "failed to enable supply: %d\n", err);
+			return err;
+		}
 	}
 
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(p->enable_gpio, 1);
-- 
2.43.0
